target:    admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
gate:      php tests/funnel-step-identity-test.php
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    caches without the !$had_error guard
rationale: When CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE ... AS SELECT fails (privilege revoked, malformed rule, deadlock), get_funnel_results() bails with $had_error and skips set_transient, so the next request recomputes. Removing the guard caches the partial result — a corrupt funnel served as a plausible zero, indefinitely on a host that revoked the privilege: the D52 silent zero at the cache layer. The gate requires the if-condition to NEGATE $had_error, so `if (true)` — which keeps the block, the call, and the comment — fails the negation requirement, not a text match.
---
diff --git a/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php b/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
--- a/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
+++ b/admin/view/wp-slimstat-db.php
@@ -2662,5 +2662,5 @@
         // Don't cache a funnel whose query errored — let it recompute next time
         // in case the failure was transient (deadlock) or the rule was fixed.
-        if (!$had_error) {
+        if (true) {
             set_transient($cache_key, $results, 5 * MINUTE_IN_SECONDS);
         }
